From fccecb80774560cef9ed32d256f3985fa1de1a2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Szewczyk <a.szewczyk@cthings.co>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:38:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] scripts: sbom: make FileName relative to the package root

Backport of upstream nrfconnect/sdk-nrf#30566 ("scripts: sbom: Make FileName
relative to the package root", Nicolae Dicu), which is still open against main.

west ncs-sbom emitted every SPDX FileName relative to the OUTPUT directory:

    relative_path(file, output_directory) -> './' + os.path.relpath(...)

so any file outside the workspace came out as a ../ ladder - a toolchain header
was recorded as ./../../../../opt/toolchains/zephyr-sdk-X/... That is both a
disclosure of the build machine's layout and wrong per SPDX 2.3 clause 8.1,
which says FileName is relative to the PACKAGE root.

Record each package's root directory and emit FileName relative to it. The
toolchain package already knows its root, and a git package's root is the
repository top level.

- data_structure: Package.root_path.
- input_build: set it on the toolchain package.
- git_info_detector: set it on a git package, from `git rev-parse
  --show-toplevel`. Upstream has a module_root to hand at this point; this
  branch does not, so it is derived here with a helper shaped like get_sha().
- output_template: package_roots(), strip_anchor() and spdx_file_name() are
  taken verbatim from upstream, including the fallback chain - package root,
  else the workspace-relative path when it does not escape the workspace, else
  the absolute path with its anchor stripped.
- raport.spdx.jinja: call spdx_file_name(file) instead of
  relative_path(file.file_path).

Function names and bodies are kept identical to upstream so that adopting the
merged version is a revert of this patch rather than a merge.

This covers the SPDX output only, as upstream's change does. report.html.jinja
still emits file_path verbatim inside a file:/// link, so the .html half of an
SBOM continues to carry absolute paths and still needs scrubbing after
generation.

